The '''Saleebaan Period''' ([[Burawi language|Burawi]]: ''Xilligii Saleebaan'') was the fourth and final era of the [[Kingdom of Ufyen]], spanning approximately 400 to 900 AD. It encompasses four dynasties — the '''Saleebaan''', '''Rooble''', '''Samatar''', and '''Guri''' — and is characterised by the kingdom's response to the formation of the [[Kingdom of Burawa]], progressive territorial contraction, and the final conquest of the Ufyen state.

